ns 4.1 and 7.6.2 the private\n  1986\t    engine-resource table of section 7.3, and a parked entry of each\n  1987\t    kind lifts and lowers through UCF's round-trip test.\n  1988\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1989\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name`,\n  1990\t    discards unproven assertions as `:unauthenticated`, and ignores\n  1991\t    undeclared principals, at a fixed snapshot.\n  1992\t15. A module that defines a name and then reads it in the main\n  1993\t    sequence produces no obligation for that name; a main-sequence\n  1994\t    read before the definition is `:use-before-definition`; a read\n  1995\t    inside a body is free of obligation only when an unconditional\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Both r7 objections appear addressed in the new wording. I’m checking one consequence of moving handles into a private resource table: whether an exported closure’s stream references can still be transferred into the receiving task."}}
