ocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1091:`dao.lease.md`'s \"fencing from the resource\" for durable resources, and it\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1169:end the prior tenure). Its inventory of possessed resources is the set of\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1187:   refusal; compute `:yin.k/requires` and `:yin.k/store` by the fixed point\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1207:4. Evaluate `:yin.k/requires` (§7.6.5); fetch what may be fetched (segments\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1219:7. **Restore into an isolated store** (§7.6.2): the slice, the remapped\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1247:| `:yin.k/non-portable` | lift | `:yin.k/path`, `:yin.k/kind`, `:yin.k/hint` — kinds at §7.5.4, cycles included as `:kind :cyclic` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1270:| No hidden global state | Every dependency is declared in `:yin.k/requires` — *as computed by the declared fixed point, with its completeness stated* (`:yin.k/discovery`); the store travels as an explicit slice restored into an isolated store; fresh-name state and parked records travel explicitly; custody is facts on a named, possessed medium. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
