{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1960,1990p;1820,1845p;1758,1825p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1758\t\n  1759\tThe scheduler registry's `:modules` map changes from `{name {sym fn}}`\n  1760\tto `{name {:manifest m :address a :derivation d :slice {sym encoded}\n  1761\t:stores {addr encoded}}}` -- the portable act-1 encoding, never\n  1762\tlowered values (section 7.3, act 4). Each task's own `:modules`\n  1763\tentry gains\n  1764\tthat task's lowered `:bindings` and `:module-stores` instance when\n  1765\tits require completes; `resolve-var` reads task state, so no task\n  1766\tresolves through another task's coordinates or store. No shim keeps\n  1767\tthe old entry shape: this is a dev-only repository with no deployed\n  1768\tregistries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1769\t\n  1770\t## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n  1771\t\n  1772\tFive steps, each landing green on all three hosts before the next. The\n  1773\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1774\t\n  1775\t```mermaid\n  1776\tflowchart TD\n  1777\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1778\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1779\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1780\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1781\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1782\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1783\t```\n  1784\t\n  1785\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1786\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1787\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1788\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1789\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1790\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1791\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1792\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1793\t\n  1794\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1795\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1796\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1797\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1798\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1799\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1800\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1801\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1802\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1803\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1804\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1805\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1806\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1807\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1808\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1809\t`:blake3`.\n  1810\t\n  1811\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1812\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1813\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1814\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1815\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1816\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1817\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1818\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1819\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1820\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1820\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1821\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1821\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1822\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1822\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1823\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1823\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1824\t\n  1824\t\n  1825\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1825\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1826\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1827\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1828\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1829\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1830\tundeclared principal is ignored; a signed retraction bound to an\n  1831\tassertion's id removes that assertion only, and a retraction naming no\n  1832\tassertion or signed by another principal is discarded; an exact\n  1833\tduplicate envelope is honored once and never counted as equivocation;\n  1834\ta replayed sequence and a distinct equivocating pair are discarded; two\n  1835\tproven assertions refuse `:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then:\n  1836\tthe manifest and derivation\n  1837\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1838\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1839\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1840\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1841\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1842\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1843\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1844\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1845\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1960\t\n  1961\t5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n  1962\t   formats where applicable, through both `fetch` and `step`.\n  1963\t6. A payload whose address is valid but whose identity is not the one\n  1964\t   requested is refused for every format, including the two whose\n  1965\t   identity is a storage address, and under every registered algorithm.\n  1966\t7. A request naming a contract the format record does not implement is\n  1967\t   `:contract-mismatch` before validation runs.\n  1968\t8. A malformed row is refused before any of its children is requested,\n  1969\t   and every composition bound produces `:parts-limit`.\n  1970\t9. Local `fetch` produces exactly the content-pair traffic the stepped\n  1971\t   path produces and holds no content handle.\n  1972\t\n  1973\tRequire:\n  1974\t\n  1975\t10. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\n  1976\t    parks, links, installs through the child phases, and resumes with\n  1977\t    `'foo`; the same over the JVM WebSocket content path.\n  1978\t11. The scheduler registry holds no function that arrived by linking\n  1979\t    and no lowered bindings, only the portable slice; every task-local\n  1980\t    `:bindings` was lowered from a slice an isolated child evaluation\n  1981\t    produced, which reached halt with every export bound.\n  1982\t12. UCF section 7.4.1 carries `:link-request`, `:link-response`, and\n  1983\t    `:install` safepoints, section 7.4.3 their pending variants, section\n  1984\t    7.5.1 the `:yin.k/binding` closure variants and `:yin.k/store-of`\n  1985\t    key of section 7.3, sections 4.1 and 7.6.2 the private\n  1986\t    engine-resource table of section 7.3, and a parked entry of each\n  1987\t    kind lifts and lowers through UCF's round-trip test.\n  1988\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1989\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name`,\n  1990\t    discards unproven assertions as `:unauthenticated`, and ignores\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
