{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -42\"","aggregated_output":"1:## §7. The Universal Continuation Format (Proposed)\n18:# Universal Continuation Format — protocol draft\n37:## §7.1 Stance: a continuation is a value, not a session\n76:## §7.2 Vocabulary and envelope\n131:## §7.3 Code identity — content-addressed semantic profiles (blocker 5)\n133:### 7.3.1 The problem restated as data\n139:### 7.3.2 The canonical instruction vector and its address\n239:### 7.3.3 The contract stamp\n276:### 7.3.4 References to code inside a continuation\n350:## §7.4 Safepoints — where a canonical configuration exists (blocker 1)\n352:### 7.4.1 Only safepoints lift, and the table is the machine's\n408:### 7.4.2 Safepoint maps for foreign engines: static facts only\n465:### 7.4.3 The pending wait travels as data — complete, and resumable elsewhere\n539:## §7.5 Recursive portable encoding (blocker 2)\n541:### 7.5.1 A disjoint tagged grammar\n595:### 7.5.2 Primitives: a name is a binding, not a meaning\n650:### 7.5.3 Sharing, cells, and cycles\n717:### 7.5.4 Failure is total and names its place\n740:## §7.6 Dependency closure and context (blocker 3)\n742:### 7.6.1 Declared, not hand-written — and discovered conservatively\n812:### 7.6.2 The store slice, restored as an isolated store\n849:### 7.6.3 The migration unit is one task\n881:### 7.6.4 Modules\n894:### 7.6.5 The satisfaction check\n922:## §7.7 Ownership arbitration — custody as a lease over datoms (blocker 4)\n924:### 7.7.1 The race, named\n939:### 7.7.2 Custody facts, and their dispatch keys\n973:### 7.7.3 The authority: what the grantor possesses\n1019:### 7.7.4 The exporting state: fencing the source before publication\n1069:### 7.7.5 Fencing effects: epochs, operation ids, and what exactly-once costs\n1149:### 7.7.6 Successors and chains\n1165:### 7.7.7 Restart\n1175:## §7.8 Lifecycle: lift on park, lower on resume\n1237:## §7.9 Outcome algebra\n1266:## §7.10 Invariant compliance\n1286:## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
