{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '246,283p;1918,1933p'\"","aggregated_output":"   246\t\n   247\t### 4.1 The format record\n   248\t\n   249\tA format record is a plain map held in linker-local state. B6 fixed three\n   250\tfunction slots; this revision replaces one, renames one, and adds four:\n   251\t\n   252\t```clojure\n   253\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code      ; the dispatch key\n   254\t :contract            \"b1\"                    ; contract revision name\n   255\t :identity-fn         (fn [value] identity)   ; mint: publish! only\n   256\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [identity value] boolean) ; step 3\n   257\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 2, per part\n   258\t :validate-fn         (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 4, whole\n   259\t :obligations-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\n   260\t :definitions-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\n   261\t :applications-fn     (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\n   262\t :parts-fn            (fn [value] [address ...])}   ; step 2 worklist\n   263\t```\n   264\t\n   265\t- `:identity-fn` mints an identity from a payload. It is used by\n   266\t  `publish!` and never by verification.\n   267\t- `:identity-matches-fn` is the step-3 check, directed by the identity.\n   268\t  For H and R it is `(= identity (image-hash value))`, a contract-pinned\n   269\t  hash with one algorithm. For the storage-derived formats it is\n   270\t  `(jing/segment-matches? identity value)`, so a value minted under\n   271\t  `:sha256` while the default is `:blake3` verifies under the algorithm\n   272\t  the identity names and never fails spuriously.\n   273\t- `:row-defect-fn` validates one fetched part on its own, before any\n   274\t  address it references is enqueued: tag, arity, slot kinds, saturation.\n   275\t  For single-payload formats it is the whole validator, run early.\n   276\t- `:parts-fn` returns the storage addresses a fetched payload references\n   277\t  and without which it is incomplete. For the three single-payload\n   278\t  formats it returns nothing. For `:yin.ast/code` it returns the child\n   279\t  row ids of a row body.\n   280\t- `:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, and `:applications-fn` are\n   281\t  **position-bearing scanners** with one shared result shape:\n   282\t\n   283\t  ```clojure\n  1918\t                                   the four streams)          (M4, M5)\n  1919\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n  1920\t            (section 7.4.1 rows, 7.4.3 variants, 7.5.1 marker\n  1921\t             keys :yin.k/binding and :yin.k/store-of)              (M4)\n  1922\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n  1923\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n  1924\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names, primitive-profiles)\n  1925\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n  1926\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1927\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1928\tMust not change:\n  1929\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1930\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing. No kernel's step function\n  1931\t          changes its decode, dispatch, or register model; the\n  1932\t          behavioral amendments r6 and r7 make at a kernel are\n  1933\t          closure-directed resolution and store routing, the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
